text:
“Mr. Beebe!” said the maid, and the new rector of Summer Street was shown in;
he had at once started on friendly relations, owing to Lucy’s praise of him in
her letters from Florence.

Immediately he realized that of all the conceited, ludicrous, contemptible ways
of announcing an engagement this was the worst. He cursed his love of metaphor;
had he suggested that he was a star and that Lucy was soaring up to reach him?

One looked down one’s nose at this. “Then certainly I won’t play,” said Cecil,
while Miss Bartlett, under the impression that she was snubbing George, added:
“I agree with you, Mr. Vyse. You had much better not play. Much better not.”

“From the red gold keep thy finger; 
Vacant heart and hand and eye 
Easy live and quiet die.”
